Fix buffer parameters and object lifecycle for real-world pipeline
handlers and session managers.

- Never publish a fixed SPA_PARAM_BUFFERS_size of 0 (OpenBSD uvideo(4)
  VIDIOC_TRY_FMT reports sizeimage of the not yet allocated frame
  buffer, leaving streamConfig.frameSize at 0).
- Encode the plane offset within the fd as mapoffset, not
  chunk->offset: planes of several buffers may share one fd and
  consumers apply chunk->offset inside the already plane-sized
  mapping, crashing on the first buffer with a non-zero offset.
- Update chunk->size per frame from FrameMetadata bytesused (essential
  for MJPEG).
- Add a destructor with full teardown: destroying a node while it
  holds the camera acquisition (e.g. the session manager recreating a
  node after an error) leaked the acquisition forever, making every
  new node instance for the camera fail with -EBUSY.
- Free the request pool and frame buffer allocator when buffers are
  cleared in port_use_buffers, otherwise a later buffer renegotiation
  fails allocBuffers() with -EBUSY.

